(2) In considering a promotion, the following factors shall be taken into account—

(a) Efficiency;

(b) Requisite qualifications;

(c) Seniority;

(d) Experience;

(e) Sense of responsibility;

(f) Initiative;

(g) Power of leadership;

(h) Power of expression;

(i) Relations with staff;

(j) Co-operation with members of administration;

(k) General attitude to work of the Service, i.e. re-sourcefulness, willingness to undertake other
assignments in times of crisis—quality of independent action in taking decision, power of
leadership; and

(1) General conduct.
